7
00:00:23,080 --> 00:00:24,220
Stage a fake fire drill?

8
00:00:24,680 --> 00:00:25,500
Set off a smoke bomb?

9
00:00:26,140 --> 00:00:26,580
Hire a stripper?

10
00:00:27,820 --> 00:00:29,900
Sir, if I could afford a strip, or I wouldn't.

11
00:00:31,080 --> 00:00:32,500
I'm not planning anything.

12
00:00:32,840 --> 00:00:34,980
I signed up for the test because I really want to take it.

13
00:00:35,180 --> 00:00:36,280
Hold your ponies.

14
00:00:37,560 --> 00:00:42,080
You expect me to believe that you, Ben Siever, are college bound?

15
00:00:42,200 --> 00:00:42,980
Yes, I am.

16
00:00:43,000 --> 00:00:44,300
That's why I want to take the test.

17
00:00:44,600 --> 00:00:46,760
But, Mr. Siever, you're a pathetic student.

18
00:00:47,320 --> 00:00:50,740
The only person with worse grades than you is that kid who got hit by lightning.

19
00:00:51,960 --> 00:00:53,720
This year I'm doing much better than Sparky.

20
00:00:54,480 --> 00:00:55,740
Please, check my grades.

21
00:01:01,340 --> 00:01:03,340
A 3.0.

22
00:01:04,480 --> 00:01:06,560
Miss Dexter, put down that bottle.

23
00:01:09,140 --> 00:01:11,060
Someone has cracked the computer security code.

24
00:01:11,600 --> 00:01:13,140
All I've been cracking lately is books.

25
00:01:13,260 --> 00:01:15,260
If you don't believe me, please ask my teachers.

26
00:01:16,500 --> 00:01:17,080
Luck I am.

27
00:01:19,500 --> 00:01:20,280
All right, Mr.

28
00:01:20,500 --> 00:01:23,780
Seaver, I am going to give you the application for the exam.

29
00:01:24,700 --> 00:01:27,940
But if I find out you have been tampering with your grades...

30
00:01:28,560 --> 00:01:30,160
Sir, I haven't tampered with anything.

31
00:01:30,880 --> 00:01:34,220
I swear that I, Ben Siever, am a 3.0 student.

32
00:01:34,500 --> 00:01:42,560
Believe me. Brianne, what are you doing?

33
00:01:43,140 --> 00:01:45,260
Carol, I'm tired of being selfish.

34
00:01:45,660 --> 00:01:48,700
I have made a decision that will change both of our lives.

35
00:01:48,920 --> 00:01:51,080
You're gonna pick up your toenails after you clip them?

36
00:01:51,940 --> 00:01:56,240
No. I finally realized that it's time I gave a little back.

37
00:01:56,860 --> 00:01:58,640
So I've taken a job in Africa.

38
00:02:01,600 --> 00:02:04,460
You're going to work in a third -world country?

39
00:02:04,640 --> 00:02:06,300
I'm not sure what number it is.

40
00:02:08,940 --> 00:02:12,360
Will you be working in hospitals, building homes, farming?

41
00:02:12,620 --> 00:02:16,860
Better. I'll be teaching low -impact aerobics at a club met in Senegal.

42
00:02:22,080 --> 00:02:25,260
Oh, you're gonna miss me.

43
00:02:25,580 --> 00:02:27,440
That hardly describes it.

44
00:02:28,260 --> 00:02:29,700
I've got a plane to catch.

45
00:02:30,760 --> 00:02:32,420
Brianne, I will never forget you.

46
00:02:32,580 --> 00:02:33,420
Don't you cry.

47
00:02:33,820 --> 00:02:34,780
I'll be strong.

48
00:02:38,000 --> 00:02:40,380
It's over! She's gone!

49
00:02:40,920 --> 00:02:44,860
Ladies and gentlemen, Brianne has left the building.

50
00:02:46,560 --> 00:02:46,840
I'm sorry, I'm sorry.

51
00:02:46,840 --> 00:02:48,800
Show me that smile.

52
00:02:48,800 --> 00:02:51,180
Ooh, show me that smile.

53
00:02:51,520 --> 00:02:55,160
Don't waste another minute on your crying.

54
00:02:55,460 --> 00:02:58,440
We're going near, near, nowhere near.

55
00:02:58,600 --> 00:03:02,260
The best is ready to begin.

56
00:03:03,020 --> 00:03:04,900
Oh, oh, oh.

57
00:03:04,900 --> 00:03:08,120
As long as we got each other,

58
00:03:08,840 --> 00:03:12,520
we got the world spinning right in our hands.

59
00:03:12,920 --> 00:03:20,340
Baby, you and me, we gotta be The luckiest dreamer to ever quit dreaming.

60
00:03:20,560 --> 00:03:23,500
As long as we keep on giving,

61
00:03:24,320 --> 00:03:28,000
we can take anything that comes our way.

62
00:03:28,320 --> 00:03:38,560
Baby rain or shine, all the time, we got each other sharing the laughter and love.

63
00:03:40,220 --> 00:03:43,680
Sharing the laughter and love.

64
00:03:51,580 --> 00:03:52,560
Hey, what's shaking?

65
00:03:53,360 --> 00:03:55,520
I'm playing a game of hide and eat with Chrissy.

66
00:03:55,940 --> 00:03:56,900
Isn't it hide and seek?

67
00:03:57,100 --> 00:03:58,520
You play your way, I'll play mine.

68
00:04:00,700 --> 00:04:02,720
The advanced placement exam.

69
00:04:03,160 --> 00:04:04,600
Ooh, smart guy.

70
00:04:04,840 --> 00:04:05,480
Keep it down.

71
00:04:05,520 --> 00:04:06,820
I don't want Vom and Dad to know.

72
00:04:07,120 --> 00:04:08,460
If I fail, nobody will be the wiser.

73
