Hey, guys. Where's Dad?

74
00:04:11,660 --> 00:04:14,040
I need to hit him up for a loan before he meets with his accountant.

75
00:04:14,220 --> 00:04:15,820
Do you think I'm made of money?

76
00:04:17,660 --> 00:04:21,900
Too late. You guys will never guess what happened.

77
00:04:22,460 --> 00:04:26,060
Brianne moved out and I'm gonna be alone for the rest of the semester.

78
00:04:26,480 --> 00:04:27,280
Oh, Carol, wake up.

79
00:04:27,360 --> 00:04:28,640
You're gonna be alone for the rest of your life.

80
00:04:31,900 --> 00:04:36,480
You guys can laugh if you want, but I'm here to pack up and leave this place

81
00:04:36,480 --> 00:04:40,020
forever. You are seeing this face for the last time.

82
00:04:40,160 --> 00:04:41,800
Does anyone want to feel that one?

83
00:04:42,820 --> 00:04:44,300
Hey, look, lighten up.

84
00:04:44,300 --> 00:04:47,520
May I remind you that Carol is very important to us?

85
00:04:47,720 --> 00:04:48,400
Oh, you're right.

86
00:04:48,420 --> 00:04:49,340
She's your sister.

87
00:04:49,540 --> 00:04:50,480
What the heck with that?

88
00:04:50,480 --> 00:04:51,980
She's got a room that you could have.

89
00:04:53,980 --> 00:04:55,220
Absolutely. It's yours.

90
00:04:55,620 --> 00:04:57,560
Carol doesn't live here anymore.

91
00:04:58,020 --> 00:05:01,120
Great. Hey, you back up the car, we'll throw your junk out the window.

92
00:05:02,480 --> 00:05:03,220
This is great.

93
00:05:03,220 --> 00:05:05,400
As soon as I get back from the library, I'm moving in.

94
00:05:07,040 --> 00:05:08,880
I thought you'd never find me.

95
00:05:09,160 --> 00:05:10,280
I thought so too.

96
00:05:10,780 --> 00:05:12,320
Okay, Ben. Now it's your turn to fly.

97
00:05:12,640 --> 00:05:20,240
Oh, goody. Ooh, coats!

98
00:05:26,940 --> 00:05:32,960
Ten, twenty, thirty, thirty, thirty, a hundred.

99
00:05:35,240 --> 00:05:37,640
I'm not falling for that one.

100
00:05:40,540 --> 00:05:46,280
I realize I'm a licensed CPA, but I'll try to explain it in layman's terms.

101
00:05:46,340 --> 00:05:49,560
See, you don't send bills, you don't get paid.

102
00:05:49,820 --> 00:05:52,320
Well, Carol used to input my dad on computer.

103
00:05:52,380 --> 00:05:53,340
Now she's away at college.

104
00:05:53,480 --> 00:05:54,880
Can't one of your other kids help?

105
