From now on, this will be our driveway.

200
00:11:38,640 --> 00:11:40,600
Can we meet right here tomorrow?

201
00:11:41,440 --> 00:11:46,600
Oh, no. I just packed up all my stuff for the dorm, gave away my room, and told my

202
00:11:46,600 --> 00:11:48,440
family they'd never see me again.

203
00:11:51,040 --> 00:11:52,320
Tomorrow it is.

204
00:12:01,680 --> 00:12:03,340
Carol, I thought you were going to New York.

205
00:12:03,680 --> 00:12:06,040
Mother, the most amazing thing has happened.

206
00:12:07,180 --> 00:12:09,240
Do you remember Dwight Halliburton from the Catskills?

207
00:12:09,520 --> 00:12:11,360
The one who kept hitting himself in the head?

208
00:12:12,420 --> 00:12:14,420
Right. And guess what?

209
00:12:14,760 --> 00:12:16,860
Now he's doing it in our neighborhood.

210
00:12:19,140 --> 00:12:22,920
He has uprooted his whole life to move near me.

211
00:12:23,940 --> 00:12:25,720
That sounds very romantic.

212
00:12:26,560 --> 00:12:28,200
Bizarre, but romantic.

213
00:12:29,180 --> 00:12:31,200
So I'll be staying here tonight.

214
00:12:31,480 --> 00:12:33,420
Oh, but Carol, you gave your room to Luke today.

215
00:12:34,080 --> 00:12:35,760
Oh. Well, that's okay.

216
00:12:36,200 --> 00:12:37,820
I'll sleep on a fold -out.

217
00:12:37,940 --> 00:12:40,240
